  "comments": [
    {
      "position": 0,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "-> negates what one would generally conclude from the previous statements or situation\n=it does not (necessarily)mean that~; it does not (necessarily) follow that~",
      "html": "-&gt; negates what one would generally conclude from the previous statements or situation<br/>=it does not (necessarily)mean that~; it does not (necessarily) follow that~",
      "credits_raw": "deeana",
      "content_sha256": "760e75d47bfad3c2413f46f895c62b56bef010e4c87dcea6a13e4691391f388b",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 1,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "＊わけではない sentences and their context (whether before or after) are often connected by conjunctions like が and しかし.\n\nFORMATION:\nいＡ + わけではない\nなＡ + な + わけではない\nＶ(plain form) + わけではない",
      "html": "＊わけではない sentences and their context (whether before or after) are often connected by conjunctions like が and しかし.<br/><br/>FORMATION:<br/>いＡ + わけではない<br/>なＡ + な + わけではない<br/>Ｖ(plain form) + わけではない",
      "credits_raw": "rubyhatchet",
      "content_sha256": "175c83ea11bd83ea4da22e73f3187a7c7a69cba80474d7c575ae526294b5e87d",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Used similarly to \"That's not to say that ___\"",
      "html": "Used similarly to \"That's not to say that ___\"",
      "credits_raw": "Amatuka",
      "content_sha256": "118f878a4e601982a9e26d0a64c2da5ee91629ed72f5bf92265666cb6b6351d2",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "I read manga for practice, and this phrase appears frequently in some form or another. I see it frequently when there has been some form of a misunderstanding (そういう訳じゃない、よ！)",
      "html": "I read manga for practice, and this phrase appears frequently in some form or another. I see it frequently when there has been some form of a misunderstanding (そういう訳じゃない、よ！)",
